{
  "title": "Tafaaul and Istekhaarah",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "Quoting the book of al-Da’waat by al-Khateeb al-Mustaghferi, Sayyed Ibn Taaoos has reported the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) to have said:\n“When you want to seek a portent (tafaaul) in the Book of Allah the Almighty and All-majestic, you may recite [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) three time, invoke Allah’s blessings upon the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) and his Household three times, and say these words:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّىْ تَفَاَّلْتُ بِكِتَابِكَ \nALLAAHUMMA INNEE TAFAA-ALTO BE-KETAABEKA \nO Allah, indeed I seek a good omen from Your Book \nوَ تَوَكَّلْتُ عَلَيْكَ فَاَرِنِىْ مِنْ كِتَابِكَ \nWA TAWAKKALTO A’LAYKA FA-ARENEE MIN KETAABEKA \nand I place my absolute trust in You; so show me from Your Book \nمَا هُوَ مَكْتُوْمٌ مِّنْ سِرِّكَ الْمَكْنُوْنِ فِىْ غَيْبِكَ.\nMAA HOWA MAKTOOMUM MIN SIRRIKAL MAKNOONE FEE GHAYBEKA.\nthat which is hidden of Your concealed secret within Your Unseen.\nYou may then open a (complete) copy of the Holy Qur’an and take the portent from the first line on the first side (i.e. of the two pages) without counting the papers or the lines.”"
}
